# === .dockerignore ===
# The GUI stand mounts the checkout at /w and copies out of it exactly one file — the package list —
# so the build context is a whitelist, not a blacklist. Without this file every build would first
# upload the whole tree (`.gomodcache` alone is gigabytes, `tmp/` and `Python/` add more), and the
# question "what does a rebuild of this image cost" would stop having an answer.
*
!stand/apt-deps.txt
